nd some low-growth/moderate-inflation mass falls to B. Step 4, B = residual = 100 - 13 - 20 - 17 = 50. CONSISTENCY CHECK PERFORMED: my CQ3 P50 of 1.90% lands squarely in B's band, so B must and does carry the plurality; I have NOT put most mass on A, as the lock warns against. My CQ2 of 29% is the China-conjoined joint, not the OECD inflation marginal, so C's 20 is not bounded by 29 — but it IS bounded by the 52% OECD marginal, and 20 < 52 x 0.54 = 28, which it satisfies. B at 50 also reads as slightly above AI-Q6's standalone Jagged-Diffusion 47.2%, which is the correct direction: adding endogenous demographics adds the physical/care-scarcity leg to the hyperscaler-rent leg, which is precisely what the barbell describes, so coupling should move mass INTO B — mostly out of A (growth cap) and partly out of the extreme Hulten tail (because the shadow-price surge in bottleneck sectors is itself inflationary growth in nominal terms).","referenceClassIds":[],"schemaVersion":"forecast-workbench.forecast/v1","sealedAt":"2026-11-04T17:31:54.353Z","seriesId":"published-panel","strongestContraryCase":"Not elicited per question. Panelist falsification signposts: {\"signpost\":\"OECD-38 health and social care job vacancy rate (Eurostat JVS + US JOLTS health care & social assistance), 4-quarter average, versus its 2025 level\",\"by_when\":\"Q4 2028\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"If care vacancy rates have FALLEN >= 25% from 2025 without an accompanying recession, my licensed-care-hours weakest link is wrong: raises CQ1 conjunct 1, raises CQ3 P50 by ~+0.15 pp, and shifts ~4 pp of CQ6 mass from C into A/B. If instead they have RISEN >= 20%, my CQ1 falls to ~12 (rationing confirmed as the clearing mechanism) and C rises ~3 pp.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Median US FERC/ISO plus EU TSO interconnection queue wait for >100 MW load, paired with a real wage index for licensed high-voltage electricians and linemen (BLS 47-2111/49-9051 and Eurostat equivalents)\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 2029\",\"if_obser